  "content": {
    "id": "p30-stem-19-26-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Solve the following for $0^{\\circ}\\leq\\theta\\leq360^{\\circ}$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p30-q19",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\cos\\theta=\\frac12$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=60^{\\circ},\\ 300^{\\circ}$.",
          "worked": "The related angle is $60^{\\circ}$. Cosine is positive in quadrants 1 and 4.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=60^{\\circ}\\\\\\theta&=360^{\\circ}-60^{\\circ}=300^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q20",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\tan\\theta=\\sqrt3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=60^{\\circ},\\ 240^{\\circ}$.",
          "worked": "The related angle is $60^{\\circ}$. Tangent is positive in quadrants 1 and 3; its solutions are $180^{\\circ}$ apart.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=60^{\\circ}\\\\\\theta&=60^{\\circ}+180^{\\circ}=240^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q21",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\theta=-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=240^{\\circ},\\ 300^{\\circ}$.",
          "worked": "The related angle is $60^{\\circ}$. Sine is negative in quadrants 3 and 4.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^{\\circ}+60^{\\circ}=240^{\\circ}\\\\\\theta&=360^{\\circ}-60^{\\circ}=300^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q22",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\tan\\theta=-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=135^{\\circ},\\ 315^{\\circ}$.",
          "worked": "The related angle is $45^{\\circ}$. Tangent is negative in quadrants 2 and 4; its solutions are $180^{\\circ}$ apart.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^{\\circ}-45^{\\circ}=135^{\\circ}\\\\\\theta&=135^{\\circ}+180^{\\circ}=315^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q23",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\cos\\theta=-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=150^{\\circ},\\ 210^{\\circ}$.",
          "worked": "The related angle is $30^{\\circ}$. Cosine is negative in quadrants 2 and 3.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^{\\circ}-30^{\\circ}=150^{\\circ}\\\\\\theta&=180^{\\circ}+30^{\\circ}=210^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q24",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\sec\\theta=\\sqrt2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=45^{\\circ},\\ 315^{\\circ}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2}\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe related angle is $45^{\\circ}$. Cosine is positive in quadrants 1 and 4.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=45^{\\circ}\\\\\\theta&=360^{\\circ}-45^{\\circ}=315^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q25",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta=-2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=210^{\\circ},\\ 330^{\\circ}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sin\\theta&=-\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe related angle is $30^{\\circ}$. Sine is negative in quadrants 3 and 4.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^{\\circ}+30^{\\circ}=210^{\\circ}\\\\\\theta&=360^{\\circ}-30^{\\circ}=330^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q26",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$\\cot\\theta=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=120^{\\circ},\\ 300^{\\circ}$.",
          "worked": "The given cotangent is nonzero, so both sine and cosine are nonzero and reciprocal conversion is valid.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\theta&=-\\sqrt3\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe related angle is $60^{\\circ}$. Tangent is negative in quadrants 2 and 4.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^{\\circ}-60^{\\circ}=120^{\\circ}\\\\\\theta&=120^{\\circ}+180^{\\circ}=300^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      }
    ]
